== Targetable ==
=== Clone ===
A '''clone''' is a copy of a champion that is considered a champion for the purposes of targeting and interacting with most non-{{tip|takedown}} effects, but otherwise considered a {{tip|pet}}. The damage of a '''clone''' credited to the owner for the purposes of {{tip|turret}} aggro, but is considered their own for interactions with other effects. Depending on the creation, a clone can copy almost almost all effects from the owner, such as item bonuses and current inflicted [[debuff]]s.

Clones inherit all [[item]] stats and passive effects. Clones do not generally interact with [[rune]]s, but may inherit some buffs granted by runes on a case-by-case basis.

[[Takedown]]s scored by '''clones''', including those against non-champions, are attributed to their owner.
<!--this used to say clones are separate combat sources, but that should be obvious since they do their own damage and it's already mentioned on the combat page-->

The damage dealt by a clone's basic attacks is not considered to be [[ability damage]] and so '''will not''' trigger [[spell effects]] (e.g. {{ii|Liandry's Torment}}, {{ii|Luden's Echo}}). Some clones can {{tip|heal}} themselves with {{stil|life steal}} if they have any.<!--this used to also say their ATTACKS trigger support item, but they don't trigger the execute it's just that their kills count as yours-->

;Controllable
: ''The player can control the following clones' actions to an extent. This is possible by using the [[hotkey]] assigned to ''Move Pet Click'' orders or to the ability that summoned them.''
* {{cai|Mirror Image|LeBlanc}}
** Controls movement and basic attacks without dealing damage but applying some on-hit effects.
* {{cai|Hallucinate|Shaco}}
** Controls movement and basic attacks while also applying any cloned on-hit effects. Can mimic Shaco's ability animations, emotes and {{si|Recall}} visual effects.
* {{cai|Warrior Trickster|Wukong}}
** Controls basic attacks and can mimic Wukong's abilities.
* {{cai|Shapesplitter|Neeko}}
** Controls movement to send to another destination while the clone is active. Can mimic Neeko's ability animations, emotes, and {{si|Recall}} channel.

;Uncontrollable
: ''The player cannot control the following clones' actions.''
* {{cis|Fiddlesticks}} {{ii|Scarecrow Effigy}}
** ''Reveals'' the area and performs a random action after being {{tip|sight|seen}} by a nearby enemy champion.
* {{cai|Test of Spirit|Illaoi}}
** Does not perform any actions but is vulnerable to damage, which is transferred to its "body" (i.e. the champion it is tethered to).
* {{cai|Iceborn Subjugation|Lissandra}}
** Summons clones from slain enemy champions that chase nearby enemies for 4 seconds, dying afterwards.
* {{cai|Nimbus Strike|Wukong}}
** Creates two clones that dash to enemies around the target. {{tip|Untargetable}} during the dash, but become targetable for {{fd|0.25}} seconds by non-targeted effects after reaching their targets.

=== Minion ===
A {{tip|Minion}} is a champion-summoned unit that some champions can create. Each summoning champion can only summon their unique minions. These units exist independently of their summoning champion, but usually, will only stay summoned for a limited amount of time or as long as the summoning champion is in the immediate vicinity. These units have stats including health, which is independent from that of the summoning champion. These units may have their attacks and stats increase based on the stats of the summoning champion, but they may also be static. All damage dealt by these units is credited to the summoning champion.

;Controllable
: ''The player can control the following pets' movement. This is possible by using the [[hotkey]] assigned to ''Move Pet Click'' orders or to the ability that summoned them.''
* {{cai|Summon Tibbers|Annie|Tibbers}}
** Damages enemies around him every second, which is classified as ability damage. Can gain {{ai|Molten Shield|Annie}}.
* {{cai|Daisy!|Ivern|Daisy}}
** Can be shielded by {{ai|Triggerseed|Ivern}} and will prioritize targets hit by {{ai|Rootcaller|Ivern}}.

;Autonomous
: The following units behave autonomously.
* {{cai|Sentry|Aphelios|Lunar Sentry}}
* {{cai|Death in Lavender|Bel'Veth|Void Remoras}}
* {{cai|Spider Queen|Elise|Spiderlings}}
* {{cai|H-28G Evolution Turret|Heimerdinger}} and {{ai|H-28Q Apex Turret|Heimerdinger}}
** Turrets periodically fire a laser beam that is classified as ability damage.
* {{cai|Prophet of an Elder God|Illaoi|Tentacles}}
** Tentacles do not have basic attacks but instead perform autonomously a {{Ai|Tentacle Smash|Illaoi|Slam}} every 10 seconds at a {{ai|Test of Spirit|Illaoi|Spirit}} or a {{ai|Vessel|Illaoi}} or when commanded by Illaoi with {{ai|Harsh Lesson|Illaoi}}. The damage is classified as ability damage.
* {{cai|Void Swarm|Malzahar|Voidlings}}
* {{cai|We Are More|Naafiri|Packmates}}
** Will dynamically follow Naafiri, attacking alongside her and occasionally execute minions under a certain health threshold.
* {{cai|Awakening|Yorick|Mist Walkers}}
** Will leap toward and prioritize enemies hit by {{Ai|Mourning Mist|Yorick}}.
* {{cai|Eulogy of the Isles|Yorick|Maiden of the Mist}}
** Will stop to assist Yorick if he is attacked nearby.
* {{cai|Cell Division|Zac|Bloblets}}
** Due to this effect, {{ci|Zac}} is the only champion that can be killed by {{si|Smite}} and can be targeted and granted {{tip|invulnerability}} by {{si|Teleport}}.
* {{cai|Deadly Spines|Zyra|Thorn Spitters}} and {{ai|Grasping Roots|Zyra|Vine Lashers}}


=== Structures / Terrain ===
The individual units that make up the terrain sometimes have visible [[health bar]]s (similar to lane minions) in [[Spectator Mode]] or briefly upon initially being summoned; and can sometimes be clicked upon to view their target frame, offering arbitrary statistical information. Aside from the aforementioned bug, terrain usually cannot be selected as a target directly for exceptional cases.

Although {{cai|Magical Journey|Bard}} is functional on static terrain, it cannot be created on player-created terrain.

